{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535491 17592186045443] [17592186392266 "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535491 17592186045443] [17592186392402 "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A